name: 🤝 Project Collaboration Proposal
description: Propose a new collaborative project, define its scope, deliverables, and request contributors.
title: "[Project] <Project Name>"
labels: ["collaboration", "project-proposal"]
assignees: []
body:
  - type: markdown
    attributes:
      value: |
        Thank you for proposing a collaborative project! Please fill out the details below as thoroughly as possible to help others understand the scope and join the effort.
        
  - type: textarea
    id: background
    attributes:
      label: 0. Project Background
      description: Why is this project needed? What problem does it solve? Provide the context and motivation.
      placeholder: |
        - Current state: ...
        - Problem to solve: ...
        - Expected impact: ...
    validations:
      required: true

  - type: input
    id: project_name
    attributes:
      label: 1. Project Name
      description: A clear and concise name for the project.
      placeholder: e.g., Next-Gen NoC Router Optimization
    validations:
      required: true

  - type: dropdown
    id: project_type
    attributes:
      label: 2. Project Type
      description: What kind of collaboration is this?
      options:
        - Code Development
        - Documentation / Translation
        - Design / UI / UX
        - Testing / QA
        - Research / Academic
        - Other (Please specify in the description)
    validations:
      required: true

  - type: textarea
    id: project_plan
    attributes:
      label: 3. Project Plan
      description: Outline the timeline, milestones, and high-level execution strategy.
      placeholder: |
        - Phase 1 (Month 1): ...
        - Phase 2 (Month 2-3): ...
        - Final Deadline: ...
    validations:
      required: true

  - type: dropdown
    id: project_direction
    attributes:
      label: 4. Project Direction
      description: Select the primary technical focus area for this project.
      options:
        - AI
        - NoC (Network-on-Chip)
        - Security
        - CPU Performance Optimize
        - Verification
        - Other
    validations:
      required: true

  - type: textarea
    id: deliverables
    attributes:
      label: 5. Committed Project Deliverables
      description: List the specific, tangible outputs you commit to delivering. (e.g., source code, test reports, documentation).
      placeholder: |
        - [ ] Deliverable 1: ...
        - [ ] Deliverable 2: ...
        - [ ] Deliverable 3: ...
    validations:
      required: true

  - type: input
    id: project_link
    attributes:
      label: 6. Project Link
      description: Provide the full URL to the project repository, branch, or tracking board.
      placeholder: e.g., https://github.com/OpenXiangShan/XiangShan
    validations:
      required: true

  - type: input
    id: project_tutorial
    attributes:
      label: 7. Project Tutorial
      description: Provide the full URL to the tutorial or onboarding guide for this project.
      placeholder: e.g., https://github.com/OpenXiangShan/XiangShanLab/tree/master/xiangshan-course
    validations:
      required: true

  - type: markdown
    attributes:
      value: |
        ---
        **📌 Submission Note:** 
        It is highly recommended to submit your final project deliverables to the XiangShan Lab Course repository:
        **https://github.com/OpenXiangShan/XiangShanLab/tree/master/xiangshan-course**

  - type: checkboxes
    id: confirmation
    attributes:
      label: Proposer Confirmation
      options:
        - label: I confirm this project complies with the repository's open-source license and Code of Conduct.
          required: true
        - label: I agree to act as the project lead, maintaining progress and coordinating with contributors.
          required: true
        - label: I understand that final deliverables are recommended to be submitted to the XiangShan Lab Course repository at https://github.com/OpenXiangShan/XiangShanLab/tree/master/xiangshan-course.
          required: true
